sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Gasterosteus doryssus_early at 33 µm (10.02 Ma) faithfully reproduces Gasterosteus doryssus_early morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gasterosteus doryssus_early specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/gasterosteus_doryssus_early_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Gasterosteus doryssus_early; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics. | Hunt, Bell & Travis (2008) and Bell, Travis & Blouw (2006): pelvic reduction along the Truckee G. doryssus series, complete pelvis at the start. | Stuart, Travis & Bell (2020): Pitx1 in that fossil lineage. Nakamasu et al. (2009) and Kondo & Miura (2010): teleost chromatophore Turing patterns.; reconstructed_in_script: Early-chronospecies Schnakenberg field at λ near 32.86 µm, equal-diffusion ablation, D_u sweep, diffusion-ratio sweep, four-seed ensemble, and a successor integration at D_u × (41.50/32.86)^2. | m=2 ocellus GIF whose amplitude follows RMS(u), CV 85.9 against the gallery photograph.; transfer_boundary: 32.86 µm is the assigned cellular-detail rung, not a spacing published by Bell, Hunt, or Stuart. | The successor diffusivity scaling is a model of wavelength lengthening tied to pelvic reduction, not a measurement at 10.01 Ma. | The gallery spiral is not a Truckee thin section. Its 81.08 µm band is not λ_c.; does_not_claim: An emergent PDE spiral, a second assessor, a machine-checked Lean build, or a signed nanopublication.]; phenomenon_size: 32 µm (3.168e-05 m, log10=-4.499 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 32 µm to 9.9 cm): 32 µm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-bioelectric-polarity, 118 µm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-vertex-packing, 2.2 mm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength, 4.1 mm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-clock-wavefront, 9.6 mm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-elastic-buckling, 1.3 cm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-morphogen-condensation, 1.7 cm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-flux-canalization, 2.2 cm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41559-020-01287-x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1558-5646.2007.00310.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1666/05026.1> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

